**REST:** Multiple endpoints, each returns a fixed data shape. Client adapts to what the server returns.

`GET /api/users/1` → always returns full user object
`GET /api/users/1/posts` → separate request

**GraphQL:** Single endpoint, client specifies exactly what fields it wants.

```graphql
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    name
    posts { title }
  }
}
```

When to use which:
- REST: simple APIs, caching via HTTP, smaller teams
- GraphQL: complex data needs, mobile apps (bandwidth), multiple related resources in one request

Neither is universally better — it depends on the problem.

